  "result": "I fixed it: completion now handles arguments containing `#` correctly. The new tests fail without the fix and pass with it, and the full suite passes (1913 passed, 102 skipped).\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` built a `shlex.shlex` object directly, and by default that treats `#` as the start of a comment. Everything after an unquoted `#` was dropped, so `cli a#1` was split as `[\"cli\", \"a\"]` and completion ran on the wrong word.\n\n**Fix:** one line in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. It turns off comment handling (`lex.commenters = \"\"`), which is what `shlex.split()` already does by default.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `tests/test_parser.py`: three new `split_arg_string` cases (`my#file`, `#file`, and a standalone `#`). I put them here rather than in `tests/test_shell_completion.py` as the plan said, because the existing tests for this function live in this file.\n- `tests/test_shell_completion.py`: a new `test_full_complete_hash` test that runs full completion for bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell with a command named `a#1`.\n\n**Changelog:** I added an entry to `CHANGES.md` under a new \"Version 8.5.1 / Unreleased\" heading, since 8.5.0 is already released.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
